grexa (1.10.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bound per-tab result snapshots (tab limit + aggregate row budget) and stop
    duplicating the active tab's rows on restore; fixes the session-long memory
    growth that forced a restart.
  * Coalesce search-result streaming to one GUI update per frame, throttle
    counter updates, reuse result-list delegates, and drop the per-search O(n)
    recount to keep the UI responsive on large searches.
  * Enforce the result cap inside the scan loop, cap match-preview length, and
    thread cancellation into per-line matching.
  * Cap and cancel the literal/case-insensitive/normalized replace collectors
    and bound capture expansion to the per-file deadline.

